Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/app_provider.c
Line: 131
Function: opt_provider_param
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: If no provider is specified in -provparam (p.name == NULL) and no providers are loaded (so p.found remains 0), the code prints p.name using "%s" in the "No provider named" message, which can dereference NULL and crash.

